What:		/sys/class/input/input(x)/data_logger/requested_logger_srcs
Date:		June 2026
Contact:	patches@opensource.cirrus.com
Description:
		Allows user to set which logging sources are configured for use.

		Uses a bitmask to determine which logger sources are set and will
		be enabled when logger_en is set (0x3F will set all possible sources).

		Prints text of logger sources that are requested by the user. Logging
		cannot be enabled for sources that are not available in the loaded
		firmware. See available_logger_srcs to determine which sources can
		be configured. Sources that are built-in to the firmware and not
		configured by the driver cannot be disabled.

		Access: Read, Write

		Valid values: Represented as hexadecimal bitmask
			Bit 0: BEMF
			Bit 1: VBST
			Bit 2: VMON
			Bit 3: EP
			Bit 4: IMON
			Bit 5: PWR

